# Day 24

**22km / 7.5 hours**

As I write this the rain has returned and is pattering down on the shelter under which I sit. Even as it grows heavier I remain unconcerned, both because my tent is already setup so the grass under it will not suffer and confident that the rain will pass. Still it makes the grass and ground generally more damp and they're pretty saturated anyway. 

The day began with a shower too. I found it hard to sleep from the noise, both the intermittent rain in the night and the cars driving past. I was at a campsite very close to State Highway 1 and it turns out that's quite a commonly used road. Still just like every shower throughout the day it passed by and I could pack up my tent and set off.

I was tired from the previous day but not so badly and the section ahead was much more comfortable walking as it was primarily on the road. There was forestry and farming to pass over and by, two of the primary industries in these parts but they were comfortable as long as the cows weren't too aggressive. 

![The hills from the forestry operations scarring the land](./forestry-hills.jpg)

There was some mud around but nothing comparable to the previous day and the elevation was comfortable to traverse, the weather was colder than it has been but I was more prepared for it so it was much more manageable.

![The flowers with a nice view in the background](./flowery-view.jpg)

While writing this the shower passed and a new one set in only to also pass by, which is an example of the weather the whole day. There have been stretches of nice sunshine but also clouds and rain. My right foot's big toe is in pain while walking which severely reduced my mobility at times so I'm going that's better tomorrow. Will need a rest day at some point to let everything physical and mental recover.